  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =3(arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(0)) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
